.DS_Store

# r79 embedding caches: 308 MB, regenerable from the checkpoints in r80_panel_freeze.
# Kept out of git deliberately -- the derived per-prompt values (r79_d_*.npy) are committed.
# ⚠ 2026-08-02: these two rules were anchored `[0-9][0-9]_*/r*/`, the EAR restructure renamed
# every such directory, the rules stopped matching, and `git add -A` swept 308 MB of
# deliberately-excluded caches into a commit -- which GitHub then rejected at 106 MB. That is
# the THIRD layout-anchored pattern to fail silently in the same commit (the link checker
# certified an empty set; the meta-check hid nothing and accused nine working gates). The fix
# for all three is the same: match the THING, never the PLACE.
**/results/r79_emb_*.npy
# ...including the quarantined copies. The rule above did not match the
# _stale/ path, so 103 MB of all-NaN arrays kept the tree permanently dirty
# while looking committed-adjacent. results/_stale/WHY.md is the durable
# record of what they were; the bytes are NaN and carry nothing.
**/results/_stale/r79_emb_*.npy

# Third-party PRISM release, pulled by an adversary agent to check whether that dataset
# could carry this project's estimand (it cannot: 0 of 8,011 conversations have more than
# one rater). 153 MB of someone else's data, never ours to redistribute.
utterances.jsonl
metadata.jsonl
conversations.jsonl
survey.jsonl

# Runtime fixture batch: attack harnesses plant fake rounds here. Prefixed to match the
# campaign-anchored globs that must find them; never committed.
E99_fixtures/
99_fixtures/

# ── atlas: release-derived content must not be redistributed ──────────────────
# The remote is PUBLIC and `data/*.jsonl` is excluded above precisely so this
# repo never republishes the CoVal release. `atlas/` regenerates that release in
# a different file format -- per-prompt JSON holding every prompt, every candidate
# answer and all 28,165 annotator rationales -- so it is the SAME redistribution
# wearing a different extension. The generators are committed; their output is not.
# Rebuild with: python atlas/extract.py && extract_corpus.py && embed.py && add_geometry.py && add_layers.py
#
# ⚠ Matching the THING, not the PLACE (the lesson recorded above): these patterns
# name release-derived artefacts by what they CONTAIN, so moving atlas/ cannot
# silently re-expose them.
#
# WARNING 2026-08-05: THE PLACE-ANCHORED VERSION OF THIS BLOCK FAILED THE SAME DAY IT WAS
# WRITTEN. It listed `atlas/p/` by name; the next commit created `atlas/a/` -- 1,012 files
# holding every annotator's free text and all of their rationales -- and `git add -A atlas`
# swept them onto a PUBLIC remote. The comment directly above said "match the THING, not the
# PLACE" and the patterns underneath it did the opposite. Writing the lesson is not obeying it.
#
# So: DEFAULT-DENY the whole directory and re-admit the generators by name. A new output
# directory is now excluded BEFORE IT EXISTS, which is the only version of this rule that
# survives the next thing I build.
atlas/*
!atlas/*.py
!atlas/*.js
!atlas/*.html
!atlas/*.md
